.TH YAKITSUKE 1 "2026-10-27" "yakitsuke" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yakitsuke \- turn any video into Video CD images with readable subtitles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yakitsuke
.br
.B yakitsuke
.RI [ options ] " video " [ subtitles ]
.br
.B yakitsuke doctor
.br
.B yakitsuke version
.br
.B yakitsuke help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yakitsuke
encodes a video into VCD 2.0 BIN/CUE images, splitting it across as many
discs as it needs with a short overlap at each seam. Film stays at 23.976
frames per second, interlaced and telecined sources are detected, and every
stream is checked for Video CD conformance before an image is written.
.PP
Subtitles are burned in. Each line is measured against the picture under it
and gets a background box when that picture is bright or busy, and an outline
otherwise.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
List the tools yakitsuke needs and whether each is installed. Exits non-zero
only when a required tool is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version and the platform.
.TP
.B help
Print the usage page.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Disc
.TP
.BR \-\-cd74 ", " \-\-cd80 ", " \-\-cd90
74, 80 or 90 minute media. Default 80.
.TP
.BI \-\-disc\-minutes " N"
Explicit media length in minutes.
.TP
.BI \-\-overlap " seconds"
Footage repeated at each disc seam. Default 30.
.TP
.BI \-\-scene\-snap " seconds"
Move seams onto the nearest scene change within this many seconds; 0
disables. Default 15.
.TP
.BI \-\-title " text"
Volume label and album id. Default the file name.
.TP
.BI \-\-chapters " minutes"
An entry point every N minutes, snapped to scene changes; 0 disables.
Default 5.
.SS Picture
.TP
.BR \-\-ntsc ", " \-\-pal ", " \-\-film
Force 29.97, 25 or 23.976 frames per second. Default from the source; 24 fps
film stays film and is never duplicated.
.TP
.BR \-\-letterbox ", " \-\-crop
Fit the whole frame with bars, the default, or fill the screen.
.TP
.BI \-\-borders " auto|off"
Strip baked-in black bars first. Default auto.
.TP
.BI \-\-deinterlace " mode"
auto, on, ivtc or off. Default auto.
.TP
.BI \-\-denoise " sigma"
fftdnoiz sigma, such as 1.5. Default off.
.TP
.BR \-\-sharpen ", " \-\-no\-sharpen
Mild sharpening after the downscale. Default on.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color\-convert
Keep the source matrix instead of BT.601.
.SS Sound
.TP
.BI \-\-audio\-track " N"
Source audio stream index. Default 0.
.TP
.B \-\-normalize
EBU R128 loudness, measured first for an exact correction.
.SS Subtitles
.TP
.BI \-\-sub\-track " N"
Burn an embedded text subtitle stream.
.TP
.BI \-\-sub\-color " auto|white|yellow"
Default auto: white, yellow for black-and-white film.
.TP
.BI \-\-sub\-box " auto|always|never"
Default auto: a box behind lines on a bright or busy picture, an outline
elsewhere.
.TP
.BI \-\-sub\-offset " seconds"
Shift every subtitle; a negative value pulls them earlier.
.TP
.BI \-\-sub\-style " spec"
ASS style overrides, such as Fontsize=22.
.SS Encoder and output
.TP
.BI \-\-encoder " auto|mpeg2enc|ffmpeg"
Default auto: mpeg2enc when mjpegtools is installed.
.TP
.BI \-\-output\-dir " dir"
Destination. Default next to the source.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-mpeg
Keep the MPEG-1 program streams.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite existing images.
.TP
.B \-\-resume
Keep discs that already exist and verify.
.TP
.BI \-\-preview " seconds"
Encode one short sample from the middle.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the plan and stop.
.PP
Every option that takes a value also takes the form
.IR \-\-name = value ,
and
.B \-\-
ends the options.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B YAKITSUKE_FFMPEG
The ffmpeg to use. Otherwise the first build on the path with the filters the
run needs.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every image was written and fits its media, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR mpeg2enc (1),
.BR vcdxbuild (1)
